1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,318
Hi, I am Dhrumil Shah, and this video is

2
00:00:02,358 --> 00:00:04,188
about Phase 3 of my Mycroft project,

3
00:00:04,228 --> 00:00:06,199
where I expanded the system by building

4
00:00:06,239 --> 00:00:07,836
a modular multi-agent financial

5
00:00:07,876 --> 00:00:09,567
analytics architecture for market

6
00:00:09,607 --> 00:00:11,531
structure analysis, anomaly detection,

7
00:00:11,571 --> 00:00:13,215
peer benchmarking, tail-risk and

8
00:00:13,255 --> 00:00:14,992
liquidity analysis, and prediction

9
00:00:15,032 --> 00:00:15,740
reliability.

10
00:00:16,533 --> 00:00:18,510
Phase 3 begins with a reusable agent

11
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:20,477
framework. AgentConfig holds shared

12
00:00:20,517 --> 00:00:21,888
settings and thresholds.

13
00:00:21,928 --> 00:00:24,107
SharedContext is a namespaced blackboard

14
00:00:24,147 --> 00:00:26,174
where agents publish and require each

15
00:00:26,214 --> 00:00:27,132
other's output.

16
00:00:27,172 --> 00:00:29,199
BaseAgent adds validation, timing and

17
00:00:29,239 --> 00:00:30,813
error isolation, AgentResult

18
00:00:30,853 --> 00:00:32,829
standardises results, and AgentEvent

19
00:00:32,869 --> 00:00:34,493
keeps every action traceable.

20
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:37,491
All agents read the same validated data.

21
00:00:37,531 --> 00:00:39,469
MycroftData holds the cleaned price

22
00:00:39,509 --> 00:00:41,396
panel, returns and close matrices,

23
00:00:41,436 --> 00:00:43,272
metadata, Phase 1 predictions and

24
00:00:43,312 --> 00:00:45,352
optional Phase 2 regime labels, after

25
00:00:45,392 --> 00:00:47,380
schema checks and duplicate removal.

26
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,072
Agent one measures how tightly the 120

27
00:00:50,112 --> 00:00:51,165
names move together:

28
00:00:51,205 --> 00:00:53,032
average pairwise correlation, and the

29
00:00:53,072 --> 00:00:55,035
share of variance explained by the first

30
00:00:55,075 --> 00:00:56,811
principal component, over sixty-day

31
00:00:56,851 --> 00:00:58,313
windows ranked with expanding

32
00:00:58,353 --> 00:01:00,089
percentiles so nothing looks ahead.

33
00:01:00,129 --> 00:01:02,046
Twelve stress windows were flagged, and

34
00:01:02,086 --> 00:01:03,640
the latest window reads normal.

35
00:01:04,433 --> 00:01:06,157
Agent two scans returns, volume,

36
00:01:06,197 --> 00:01:08,264
overnight gaps and intraday range using

37
00:01:08,304 --> 00:01:10,126
rolling modified z-scores built on

38
00:01:10,166 --> 00:01:11,253
medians, not means.

39
00:01:11,293 --> 00:01:13,360
Each event is split into market, sector

40
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:15,369
and company components, then labelled

41
00:01:15,409 --> 00:01:16,986
idiosyncratic, sector-wide or

42
00:01:17,026 --> 00:01:17,770
market-wide.

43
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:19,827
It found nine thousand six hundred and

44
00:01:19,867 --> 00:01:20,905
thirty-six events.

45
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:23,607
Agent three ranks every name inside its

46
00:01:23,647 --> 00:01:25,419
own industry cohort, falling back to

47
00:01:25,459 --> 00:01:27,185
sector or the whole universe when a

48
00:01:27,225 --> 00:01:28,816
cohort is too small, then scores

49
00:01:28,856 --> 00:01:30,627
relative strength and flags laggards

50
00:01:30,667 --> 00:01:32,484
that have decoupled from their peers.

51
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:35,035
Agent four quantifies downside:

52
00:01:35,075 --> 00:01:36,963
historical value at risk, expected

53
00:01:37,003 --> 00:01:39,195
shortfall, maximum drawdown and recovery

54
00:01:39,235 --> 00:01:40,919
time, plus Amihud illiquidity.

55
00:01:40,959 --> 00:01:42,897
Documented thresholds assign a risk

56
00:01:42,937 --> 00:01:44,977
tier, and the worst component decides

57
00:01:45,017 --> 00:01:45,332
it.

58
00:01:46,133 --> 00:01:47,872
Agent five retrains nothing.

59
00:01:47,912 --> 00:01:49,706
It takes the existing holdout

60
00:01:49,746 --> 00:01:52,040
predictions and asks where they can be

61
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:54,374
trusted, segmenting by sector, regime,

62
00:01:54,414 --> 00:01:56,486
volatility quintile and risk tier.

63
00:01:56,526 --> 00:01:58,765
Every segment gets a ticker-clustered

64
00:01:58,805 --> 00:02:00,710
bootstrap interval and a label:

65
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:02,877
reliable, uncertain, unreliable, or

66
00:02:02,917 --> 00:02:04,211
insufficient sample.

67
00:02:04,251 --> 00:02:06,045
Overall is 0.516, while bull,

68
00:02:06,085 --> 00:02:08,101
high-volatility days reach 0.774.

69
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:10,716
The orchestrator runs three stages:

70
00:02:10,756 --> 00:02:12,714
market structure first, then the three

71
00:02:12,754 --> 00:02:14,665
independent analysts, then prediction

72
00:02:14,705 --> 00:02:16,569
reliability, which consumes the risk

73
00:02:16,609 --> 00:02:18,567
tiers. A failed agent degrades the run

74
00:02:18,607 --> 00:02:19,852
instead of stopping it.

75
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:22,694
Every verdict merges into one review

76
00:02:22,734 --> 00:02:24,760
queue: anomaly flag, cohort outlier,

77
00:02:24,800 --> 00:02:27,034
risk tier, model trust, market state and

78
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:28,171
a review priority.

79
00:02:28,211 --> 00:02:30,393
Human decision and rationale stay empty

80
00:02:30,433 --> 00:02:32,615
by design. This is educational research

81
00:02:32,655 --> 00:02:34,578
output, not personalised financial

82
00:02:34,618 --> 00:02:35,147
advice.

83
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:37,773
A validation suite checks schema,

84
00:02:37,813 --> 00:02:39,768
duplicates, prices, agent execution,

85
00:02:39,808 --> 00:02:41,764
output ranges, risk mathematics, AUC

86
00:02:41,804 --> 00:02:43,810
bounds and inter-agent communication.

87
00:02:43,850 --> 00:02:45,606
Thirty-three checks, all passed.

88
00:02:45,646 --> 00:02:47,751
Phase 3 expands Mycroft into a modular,

89
00:02:47,791 --> 00:02:49,946
explainable multi-agent analytics system

90
00:02:49,986 --> 00:02:51,742
where specialised agents produce

91
00:02:51,782 --> 00:02:53,788
structured evidence for human review.

92
00:02:53,828 --> 00:02:54,836
I'm Dhrumil Shah.

93
00:02:54,876 --> 00:02:56,183
Thank you for watching.
